  "proof_audit": [
    {
      "declaration": "delta / reverseTime",
      "finding": "delta is the exact strict ordered simplex predicate from the seal after T:NNReal is coerced to Real. reverseTime(T,t)(i)=T-t(Fin.rev i). A real T parameter makes the local helper more general; it does not alter the sealed NNReal horizon."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "reverseTime_involutive",
      "finding": "Two complements cancel and Fin.rev_rev restores each coordinate. The equality is pointwise on the whole ambient tuple type, including the unique empty tuple."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "reverseTime_mem",
      "finding": "Fin.strictMono_cons gives (forall i,0<t_i) and StrictMono t. Positivity after reversal uses original upper bound at i.rev; strict monotonicity uses j.rev<i.rev for i<j and order reversal of subtraction from T; the new upper bound uses original positivity. No strict-order direction is swapped incorrectly."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "reverseTime_measurable / rho_measurable",
      "finding": "Each coordinate is a measurable constant minus coordinate evaluation. measurable_pi_lambda proves ambient measurability; composition with measurable_subtype_coe and subtype_mk gives rho. No measurable-Delta hypothesis is needed merely for this subtype function measurability."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "reverseTime_volume constant-family permutation",
      "finding": "volume_measurePreserving_piCongrLeft is instantiated with the explicit constant family Fin n -> Type, i -> Real, and Fin.revPerm. The extensional equality heq specializes piCongrLeft_apply_apply at i.rev, then uses rev_rev; it handles dependent transport propositionally instead of assuming definitional reduction. Both sides have the correct (Fin n -> Real) function type. Permutation is inverse-self, so its direction is correct."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "reverseTime_volume scalar complement",
      "finding": "volume_preserving_pi applies scalar Lebesgue-preserving T-x coordinatewise. hc.comp hp means complement after coordinate permutation, exactly reverseTime. Product volume is the same standard ambient volume in the header, without density/factorial/signed determinant factor."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "rho_involutive",
      "finding": "Subtype.ext reduces the identity to the ambient involution. Proof fields carry no extra mathematical choices."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "rho_volume invariant restriction",
      "finding": "For preimage delta=delta, reverseTime_mem supplies the reverse implication; applying it a second time and the involution supplies the forward implication. restrict_preimage on ambient reverseTime_volume then has volume.restrict delta on both sides. The measurable-set hypothesis is used at the correct restriction/embedding sites."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "rho_volume exact comap and map injectivity",
      "finding": "hcoe sends literal volume.comap Subtype.val to volume.restrict delta. To prove map rho m=m, inject both measures through measurable subtype embedding. map_map rewrites map coe (map rho m) to map(coe o rho)m. This composite is definitionally reverseTime o coe, so (hr.comp hcoe).map_eq gives restricted volume. hcoe.map_eq.symm identifies the other side. No injectivity of rho is incorrectly assumed for arbitrary measure cancellation; the injective map used is the measurable embedding Subtype.val."
    },
    {
      "declaration": "zero and outside-domain cases",
      "finding": "n=0: both ambient and subtype tuple spaces are singleton; cons0 is strictly monotone vacuously and upper bounds vacuous; rho is identity and empty product volume has mass one. For n>0,T=0 (indeed T<=0), delta is empty and the subtype comap is zero. All constructors and map-injectivity arguments still apply without Nonempty or positive horizon assumptions. E/rank/normal/rate do not occur in this time-only fragment, so there is no phase restriction to import."
    }
  ],
